  "dataSourceInstructions": "\r\n## General knowledge\r\nThis source contains three tables:\r\n- `customers(customer_id PK, first_name, last_name, email UNIQUE, phone, date_of_birth, loyalty_tier, created_at)`\r\n- `flight_schedule(flight_id PK, flight_number, departure_airport, arrival_airport, departure_time, arrival_time, aircraft_type, base_fare, seat_capacity, status, created_at)`\r\n- `flight_booking(booking_id PK, flight_id FK, customer_id FK, booking_reference UNIQUE, booking_status, booking_channel, seat_number, fare_paid, taxes_and_fees, currency, payment_method, created_at)`\r\n\r\nRelationships:\r\n- `customers.customer_id` 1—* `flight_booking.customer_id`\r\n- `flight_schedule.flight_id` 1—* `flight_booking.flight_id`\r\n\r\n## Querying guidance\r\n- Join `flight_schedule` → `flight_booking` using `flight_booking.flight_id = flight_schedule.flight_id`.\r\n- Join bookings to customers using `flight_booking.customer_id = customers.customer_id`.\r\n- Availability per flight: count bookings with `booking_status IN ('Confirmed','CheckedIn')`.\r\n- Revenue per flight: sum `fare_paid + taxes_and_fees` where `booking_status <> 'Cancelled'`.\r\n- Cancelled bookings should **not** reduce revenue; no refunds modeled in this dataset.\r\n- Use `departure_time` for scheduling filters; treat it as local time for the departure airport.\r\n- Exclude results where `departure_airport = arrival_airport`.\r\n\r\n## Column selection (default)\r\n- Flights: `flight_id, flight_number, departure_airport, arrival_airport, departure_time, arrival_time, aircraft_type, base_fare, seat_capacity, status`\r\n- Bookings: `booking_id, booking_reference, booking_status, booking_channel, seat_number, fare_paid, taxes_and_fees, currency, payment_method, created_at`\r\n- Customers: `customer_id, first_name, last_name, email, loyalty_tier`\r\n\r\n## Common filters\r\n- Date ranges: `departure_time BETWEEN {start} AND {end}`\r\n- Airports: `departure_airport IN (...) OR arrival_airport IN (...)`\r\n- Status: `booking_status IN (...)` or `status IN (...)`\r\n\r\n## Examples the agent can follow\r\n1) **Available seats for a flight_number and date**\r\n   - Join schedule and bookings; group by `flight_id`; compute `available_seats`.\r\n\r\n2) **Top routes by revenue in a period**\r\n   - Group by `(departure_airport, arrival_airport)`; sum `fare_paid + taxes_and_fees` where `booking_status <> 'Cancelled'`.\r\n\r\n3) **Customer’s upcoming trips**\r\n   - Filter bookings by customer (email or ID); join to `flight_schedule`; `departure_time >= TODAY()`; order by `departure_time`.\r\n\r\n## Output format expectations\r\n- Provide a compact table (5–10 columns) and a one-sentence summary.\r\n- Include the filters used at the top (date range, airports).\r\n",
  "displayName": "flightDB",
